WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.910
Honest charts, honest reports, and a one-page dashboard.

2
00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:08.510
This is the video for module 3 of Reporting and Performance Tracking.

3
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:16.950
A good chart lets a busy reader see your main point in a few seconds. To show change over time, use a line chart.

4
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.440
To compare categories, use a column or bar chart.

5
00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:28.190
To show how a whole splits into parts, a pie chart works only with 2 to 5 slices.

6
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:34.860
And when your reader needs exact figures, like a funder checking each target, a simple table is best.

7
00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:44.020
For example, Bisi's sales were 250,000 naira in January and 262,000 in February.

8
00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:50.070
That is a real rise of 4.8%. A small, steady improvement.

9
00:00:51.320 --> 00:01:05.890
But Sheets started her chart's axis at 240,000. So January's bar showed only 10,000, and February's showed 22,000. February looked 2.2 times taller, as if sales had more than doubled.

10
00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:11.880
She fixes it in the Chart editor by setting the vertical axis minimum to 0.

11
00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:19.700
And she writes a title that states the finding: sales rose slightly in February, up 4.8%.

12
00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:30.400
Readers judge bars by their length, so always start bar and column charts at zero. Label units and dates, and check every chart on a phone screen.

13
00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:37.520
A manager or funder who catches one exaggerated number will doubt every number after it.

14
00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:43.480
Do not show only your best week. Do not change what you count without saying so.

15
00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:48.300
Do not count a woman twice because she attended two trainings.

16
00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:56.560
Always give the denominator. 30 women started businesses, out of 40 trained, or out of 400?

17
00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:10.210
And do not claim cause without evidence. Sales may have risen because of your flyer, or because December always brings more parties. Say it carefully: part of this is likely the festive season.

18
00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:24.450
For example, Halima's grant target was to train 100 women by the end of June. 82 completed. She reports 82% honestly, and does not count women who came to only one session.

19
00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:31.950
She explains the cause in one sentence: two sessions were cancelled after heavy rain flooded the venue.

20
00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:38.210
She gives evidence: the attendance registers and the venue's cancellation message.

21
00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:44.390
And she proposes a catch-up session in July, paid for with unspent venue money.

22
00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:55.410
This builds far more trust than a vague, about 100 women were reached. If you are pressured to inflate a figure, report the true number and raise the concern in writing.

23
00:02:56.660 --> 00:03:09.590
Under Nigeria's Data Protection Act 2023, personal data must be kept secure. So do not send the whole Data tab, name the women who dropped out, or post sheet links in large groups.

24
00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:24.000
Share totals, percentages and codes. Send the Summary or a PDF. Share with named email addresses as Viewer, and set sharing to Restricted, so a forwarded link does not open for strangers.

25
00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:39.970
A dashboard is one screen showing 3 to 5 KPIs against their targets. Link every cell with a formula, never type numbers in, so it updates itself. Then add green, amber and red colours with conditional formatting.

26
00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:51.180
For example, Bisi's March sales are 280,000 naira against a 300,000 target. That is 93%, so it shows amber.

27
00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:59.810
Orders are 64 against 60, and conversion is 26% against 25%. Both green.

28
00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:07.380
But repeat customers are 31% against 40%, only 78%. Red.

29
00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:19.930
So her next action is keeping customers, not more advertising. A good dashboard points to the next decision. Keep the percentage visible too, because some readers cannot tell red from green.

30
00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:27.840
To remember. Choose the chart that fits the message, start bars at zero, and let the title say the point.

31
00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:38.560
Give denominators and claim causes carefully. Report missed targets honestly, with a reason and a plan. And keep your dashboard to a few linked KPIs.

32
00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:54.250
Now practise. Make one honest chart with a title that states the finding. Audit a report against the five-point honesty check, and set your sheet to Restricted. Then build your dashboard with traffic-light colours and one trend.

33
00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:56.540
Continue with the lessons below.
